cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "pw-self-heal: In-Process Self-Healing Locators for Playwright with a Trained Similarity Ranker"
abstract: >
  pw-self-heal is an open-source TypeScript library that repairs broken
  Playwright locators at runtime, entirely in-process, with no server and no
  network dependency. When a locator resolves to zero elements, live-DOM
  candidates are scored by a trained 17-feature similarity ranker (exported to
  ONNX) and re-weighted toward the locator's expressed intent, an equivalent
  locator is rebuilt against the best match, and the action is retried. Supports
  heuristic, ML, and hybrid modes; wrapped locators remain genuine Playwright
  Locator objects so web-first assertions continue to work.
